  "title": "Path masking misses /tmp aliases and JSON-escaped forms of the worker's paths",
  "file": "src/workers/client.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker session reports a local path using a temporary-directory alias or escaped slashes. The worker sends that private filesystem path, potentially including a username, to the coordinator in events and results.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/worker-adjudication.ts\"",
    "output": "{\"probe\":\"mask\",\"scratchPrefix\":\"/private/var/\",\"eventMasked\":{\"literalCheckout\":true,\"literalScratch\":true,\"aliasScratch\":false,\"escapedCheckout\":false,\"escapedScratch\":false},\"resultMasked\":{\"literalCheckout\":true,\"literalScratch\":true,\"aliasScratch\":false,\"escapedCheckout\":false,\"escapedScratch\":false}}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe exercised HEAD's real worker loop with fake transport and harnesses; Git operations and the shared runner were mocked, with canonical scratch supplied to the harness. HEAD masks serialized data using `text.replaceAll(JSON.stringify(path).slice(1, -1), \"<worktree>\")`. Its `spellings(...)` includes supplied and canonical paths, but does not generate inverse temporary-directory aliases from canonical paths or escaped-slash variants. Both event batches and results use this sanitizer, and both leaked the tested variants. Base had no worker agent execution or reporting path. The later commit adds `agentPathMask`, explicitly expands /tmp and /var aliases in both directions, captures canonical spellings, and matches escaped slashes longest first. Running the same probe against temporary copies of the later modules reported true for every masking case."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "The worker hands the agent its scratch directory as /private/tmp/lr-XXXX/claude-501. If the session (or a tool it runs) prints that same directory as /tmp/lr-XXXX/claude-501, or prints the checkout path with escaped slashes (\\/Users\\/name\\/...), the real path goes to the coordinator unmasked. With the escaped form, that includes the worker owner's username.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun $TMPDIR/adj/s.ts  (createScratch + spellings, then the same JSON-replace reduce that runAgent's sanitize uses)",
    "output": "scratch /private/tmp/lr-qDE1QX/claude-501 spellings [ \"/private/tmp/lr-qDE1QX/claude-501\" ]\n{\"text\":\"wrote /tmp/lr-qDE1QX/claude-501/out.txt and \\\\/Users\\\\/<user>\\\\/.adjtest-OYkWqA\"}"
   },
   "evidence": "client.ts:461-467 `sanitize` replaces only `JSON.stringify(path).slice(1,-1)` for each entry of `spellings([...])`. policySpellings returns only `resolve(path)` and its realpath. createScratch already realpaths its base (`/private/tmp`), so the list has a single entry and the `/tmp` alias is never added. Escaped-slash forms are never matched either. Both alias forms need session output that spells the path differently from how it was given, which the request (\"replace the worker's checkout and scratch paths\") doesn't explicitly ask to handle. The /tmp case leaks only a random temp directory with a uid. The username leak needs a tool that escapes slashes."
  }
