  "title": "Fencing fires up to one heartbeat interval after the lease has expired",
  "file": "src/workers/client.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker loses contact with the coordinator after a delayed successful heartbeat. Its agent keeps spending quota beyond the required lease deadline until the next periodic fence check.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/worker-adjudication.ts\"",
    "output": "{\"probe\":\"fence\",\"leaseMs\":400,\"heartbeatMs\":200,\"secondHeartbeatDelayMs\":100,\"abortAfterLastSuccessMs\":501}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe exercised HEAD's real worker loop and timers with fake transport and a harness waiting for cancellation; checkout operations were mocked and no network was used. The second heartbeat succeeded after an injected 100 ms delay, and subsequent heartbeats failed. HEAD records `lastHeartbeat = performance.now()` but checks `performance.now() - lastHeartbeat > leaseMs` only inside `setInterval(..., Math.min(options.heartbeatMs ?? timing.heartbeat, leaseMs))`. Successful heartbeats do not realign that interval, leaving a systematic window beyond the deadline; cancellation occurred after 501 ms for a 400 ms lease. Base had no agent-job fence. The later commit clears and schedules a lease-duration timeout after each successful heartbeat and clears it during shutdown. The same probe against temporary copies of the later modules measured 401 ms."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A worker loses contact with the coordinator. The coordinator expires the lease after one lease period (60 s by default), but the worker only checks every heartbeat interval (10 s), so its agent session can keep spending model quota for up to about 10 s more. In that window the job may already be re-leased to another worker.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: timing-dependent; no throwaway timing harness was run here. The bound follows directly from the quoted interval code.",
   "evidence": "client.ts:552-558: `fence = setInterval(() => { if (performance.now() - lastHeartbeat > leaseMs) for (const job of agentJobs.values()) job.controller.abort(); }, Math.min(options.heartbeatMs ?? timing.heartbeat, leaseMs));`. lastHeartbeat is set only when a reply arrives (line 314). The abort therefore lands somewhere between leaseMs and leaseMs+heartbeatMs after the last success. protocol.ts sets heartbeat 10_000 and lease 60_000. The requirement is met only to within one heartbeat interval. The cost is a bounded, short overrun during a partition."
  }
